 mechanism, not a general-purpose log sink.
 
+## Totem API
+
+The totem API is a backend-for-frontend (BFF) consumed by the separate Flutter
+application. Device authentication is stateless (JWT) and scope is queue-based
+(a preset's paired device can issue tickets only to queues configured in its
+preset).
+
+### Totem pairing
+
+```text
+Operator / preset setup
+        |
+        v
+Artisan: totem:pairing-code {preset_id}
+        |
+        v
+Generate 6-digit code, set TTL = 10 min
+        |
+        v
+Display code to operator (console output)
+        |
+        v
+[Operator reads code into Flutter app]
+        |
+        v
+POST /api/totem/auth with code
+        |
+        v
+Verify preset active, code valid/unexpired/unconsumed
+        |
+        v
+Atomic: consume code, create/load Totem row, load queue scope, sign JWT
+        |
+        v
+Return JWT + entity slug/name
+```
+
+JWT lifetime (default 1h) is short; no refresh mechanism yet. On logout, the
+client discards the token (no revocation list). The backend tracks `last_seen_at`
+on every API call for operational monitoring.
+
